    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/SMjRfwN3#NdjuWh7j",
      "title": "Every frame is drawn before it is captured",
      "narrative": "The replay page reads the board only from the talk. Its glides, fades, subtitles and traffic run on a clock the renderer steps 1/30 s at a time, and even a frame a library asks of the browser runs on that clock. A frame is captured only once it is drawn and still, so no frame is held or dropped, with or without a GPU and under any load. An animation on a timeline the clock cannot stand fails the render.",
